III. PROPOSED METHODS
A. System Architecture and Sensor Deployment:
The proposed method involves designing and
implementing IoT-based system architecture for real-time
estimation of greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions. The
architecture includes a network of distributed IoT-enabled
sensors strategically deployed in key emission-intensive
areas, such as industrial facilities, transportation hubs, and
urban centers. The selection of sensor types (e.g., optical,
chemical, thermal) should be based on their ability to
measure various GHGs, including carbon dioxide (CO2),
methane (CH4), nitrous oxide (N2O), and other significant
greenhouse gases.
B. Data Acquisition and Preprocessing:
To achieve precise and robust GHG emission
estimations, advanced sensor fusion algorithms should be
employed to integrate data from multiple sensors. The sensor
fusion process involves combining information from
different sensors, considering their individual strengths,
uncertainties, and spatial distributions. Various sensor fusion
