VI. CONCLUSION
In this paper, we presented a novel and innovative approach for real-time estimation of GHG emissions using IoTintegrated sensor fusion. The proposed method provides the significance of IoT technology and advanced sensor fusion algorithms to achieve accurate and reliable real-time monitoring of GHG concentrations, including carbon dioxide (CO2), methane (CH4), and other significant GHGs. Through the experiments and performance evaluations, we demonstrated the effectiveness and practical applicability of the proposed method in diverse emission-intensive areas and environmental scenarios. The results of our study revealed that the IoT-integrated sensor fusion system provides
precise and robust GHG emission estimations, as evidenced by low MAE and RMSE values, coupled with high correlation coefficients (R) between estimated values and reference data. The real-time nature of the system enables prompt emission estimations, facilitating timely decisionmaking and swift actions to address emission hotspots and implement emission control measures. Our study emphasizes the significance of real-time GHG emission estimation in addressing climate change challenges and advancing environmental sustainability. In conclusion, the results of the proposed IoT-integrated sensor fusion method for real-time GHG emission estimation demonstrate its effectiveness, accuracy, and adaptability. The system's performance surpasses traditional monitoring techniques and showcases its potential to revolutionize GHG emission monitoring, enabling a more proactive approach to climate change mitigation. The findings presented in this paper lay the foundation for further advancements and applications of IoT technology in environmental sustainability and emission control initiatives.
